Declaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_TAtom","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L245-L246","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_TAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_TAtom","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L243-L244","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the T atom word, n = 9: [★] = -5/64. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_TFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_TFree","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L240-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_TFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_TFree","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L238-L239","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the T free word, n = 9: [★] = -1/16. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_nnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_nnAtom","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L235-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnAtom","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L233-L234","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the nn atom word, n = 6: [★] = -1/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_nnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_nnFree","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L230-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_nnFree","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L228-L229","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the nn free word, n = 6: [★] = -1/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_pnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_pnAtom","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L225-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnAtom","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L223-L224","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pn atom word, n = 6: [★] = 1/16. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_pnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_pnFree","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L220-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_pnFree","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L218-L219","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pn free word, n = 6: [★] = 1/8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_ppAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_ppAtom","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L215-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppAtom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppAtom","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L213-L214","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pp atom word, n = 6: [★] = 5/8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.star_ppFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.star_ppFree","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L210-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letters_ppFree","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L208-L209","doc":"Letter data `(w, c(σ⁽ˡ⁾))` of the pp free word, n = 6: [★] = 3/4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_step","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L179-L197","doc":"At fixed `A`, `c₁` is affine in `Z` with slope `5(2^{−A−1} − 2^{−2A}) − 8·2^{−2A}`\nwhile both species stay present (`1 ≤ Z`, `2 ≤ N`, so that after the move\n`N − 1 ≥ 1`): moving one neutron to a proton adds `5` to the census and shifts\n`I_pp − I_nn` by `2`. (At `N = 1` the truncated `I_nn` does not move and the\nshift is `1`; that boundary case is excluded here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_bond_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed_bond_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L171-L177","doc":"The `pp` and `nn` bonds differ from the `pn` bond only through the\ninterface term: `c₁(pp) − c₁(pn) = (5·(1/8 − 1/16) − 4/16)` and\n`c₁(nn) − c₁(pn) = −5·(1/8 − 1/16) + 4/16`. In particular\n`c₁(pp) + c₁(nn) = 2·c₁(pn)` — the interface contributions cancel in the\nsymmetric combination and the census terms average. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum_dyadic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum_dyadic","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L139-L147","doc":"Every [★]-shaped quantity is dyadic with denominator dividing `2^n` — the\nsame shape as the floor `c₀ = 2^{c−n}`, and the reason every measured `c₁` was\na dyadic rational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum_numerator_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum_numerator_int","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L128-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.starSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.starSum","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L124-L126","doc":"`2^{−n} Σ_ℓ w_ℓ 2^{c_ℓ}` over letter data `(w_ℓ, c_ℓ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight_values","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L118-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.letterWeight","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L110-L116","doc":"**Step 4.** The first-order weight `1 + d′(0)` of each letter type, from\n`d ∈ {0, −h, −h/2, −h(½ − δ/4)}` with `h′(0) = 2` and `δ = O(ε³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.h_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.h_dual","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L100-L108","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹` at `q = 1 + ε` is `2ε` to first order: `(1+ε)(1−ε) = 1` in the\ndual numbers, so `q⁻¹ = 1 − ε` and `h = 2ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hecke_relation_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hecke_relation_snd","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L87-L98","doc":"**Step 1, where the relation comes from.** In the dual numbers `R[ε]/(ε²)`\nthe Hecke relation `σ² = hσ + 1` for `σ = s + εX` with `h = 2ε` and `s² = 1`\nforces exactly `sX + Xs = s + s` on the `ε`-coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hecke_first_order_anticommutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hecke_first_order_anticommutes","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient.lean#L75-L85","doc":"**Step 1, ring form.** If `sX + Xs = s + s`, then `Y := X − 1` anticommutes\nwith `s`. Holds in any ring, commutative or not — and, as the linter pointed\nout, needs no `s² = 1`: that hypothesis is used only to *derive* the relation\n(`hecke_relation_snd`), not to read it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}